			"date": "2023-11-24T17:07:36.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> how the app is reading the result. So it’s probably just a normal “2 line” test with a sensor looking for the lines. </p><p>The reasoning behind that is because the sensor can prevent misreads on situations where the test line is real faint. But then you have to have some sort of reader and yeah, this situation.</p>",
